		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: New physics library - PositionBasedDynamics]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=38097#p38097"><![CDATA[
I don't think that position-based dynamics is appropriate for engineering analysis. In PBD the material behavior depends on the number of iterations, the discretization and the time step size. Hence, you won't be able to get accurate results for a specific material. PBD was developed for computer games and special effects, not for accurate simulations. However, why not use FEM with a fast solver. There exist some CG solvers on the GPU which allow to handle several thousand elements in real-time.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=818">Jan Bender</a> — Mon Aug 29, 2016 8:13 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
